  "title": "Work & School",
  "description": "Talk about common professions, school life, and daily tasks at the office.",
  "guidebook": "Welcome to the workplace and classroom! When talking about professions in Portuguese, you typically use the verb **ser** (*to be*). Note that Portuguese often omits the article when stating someone's profession directly: *Eu sou médico* (I am a doctor) or *Ela é professora* (She is a teacher).\n\nPay attention to how the preposition **em** (*in/at*) contracts with definite articles:\n- **em + o = no** (*no escritório* = in the office, *no hospital* = at the hospital)\n- **em + a = na** (*na escola* = at school, *na aula* = in class)\n\nUse *fazer* for completing tasks like *fazer o dever de casa* (to do homework)!",
